From 886d09b73767b5eee3974dd92d1eee0c49582177 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vonic <phanquochoipt@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 12:35:36 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(plugin): normalize reserved tool-call IDs before
 upstream

CLIProxyAPI synthesises tool-call IDs under the cpa_tid_v1_ namespace for the
Devin executor. Those IDs are echoed back by clients and persist in session
history, so any later turn routed to another provider carries them. mmodiary's
sub2api upstream rejects them: a captured 414KB conversation failed 400 twice
and succeeded twice once every ID was mapped to a unique portable toolu_* value.

Add a request interceptor that rewrites every reserved ID in the inbound
payload, hashing each original so an assistant tool call and its matching tool
result keep the same value.
